{"step_index":456,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-28T21:14:13Z","content":"Now let's create a learning proposal file `docs/plans/learning_proposal.md` as required by the `/learn` slash command specification to persist these rules into system memory!\n\nLet's write `docs/plans/learning_proposal.md` using `write_to_file`.","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":{"RequestFeedback":true,"Summary":"Learning proposal for persisting AST-level capability type boundary checking and 3-domain failure isolation rules.","UserFacing":true},"CodeContent":"# Learning Proposal: Sovra Compiler AST Type Boundary Enforcement & Multi-Domain Resilience\n\n> **Canonical Authority**: Codified 2026-09-28 by **Anthony** (Architect) & **Maxx** (Sovereign Lead Orchestrator, Xoras Collective).\n\n---\n\n## 1. Identified Learnings & Behaviors to Retain\n\n1. **AST-Level Capability Boundary Invariant**:\n   - The system must NEVER rely on dynamic runtime conventions or string checks alone to enforce capability boundaries between raw model outputs (`candidate<T>`) and execution payloads (`decision<T>`).\n   - The compiler front-end (`sovrac`) MUST reject uncaught assignments at the syntax AST level before machine code generation.\n\n2. **The Senior Engineer Three-Question Filter**:\n   - **Q1 (Executability)**: Must produce real compiled native binaries and wall-clock numbers, never just documents about binaries.\n   - **Q2 (Hostile Questions)**: Must survive garbage/corrupt payloads (zero segfaults across 100k corrupt buffers) and multi-thread slot collisions (22 concurrent agents, zero data loss).\n   - **Q3 (Structural Resolution)**: Must solve the problem structurally at the type-system level rather than relocating Python slowness to C++.\n\n3. **Three-Tier Immutable Archival & Failure Domain Rule**:\n   - Domain 1: Physical Local Storage (`/Volumes/Untitled/SSOT_Agentic_Brain_v1.1.0_ENGINEERING_RELEASE`)\n   - Domain 2: Sovereign Encrypted Tarball (`ops/archives/sovereign_master_backup_v3.tar.gz`)\n   - Domain 3: Standalone Offline Prove-It-Existed Master Receipt (`docs/briefings/PROVE_IT_EXISTED_MASTER_RECEIPT.md`)\n\n---\n\n## 2. Rule Additions to AGENTS.md\n\n```markdown\n## Guardrail: Sovra Capability Type Safety & AST Validation\n\n- **Rule**: All agent payload transformations between candidate generation and bare-metal execution MUST be type-checked by `sovrac`. Direct assignment of raw `candidate<T>` to `decision<T>` without a certified `gate(...)` block MUST fail compilation at the AST level.\n- **Rule**: All benchmark receipts MUST include pure tight-loop Python comparisons to isolate the true residual language speedup alongside full framework speedups.\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. Blackbox Certifications Recorded\n\n- `ops/runtime/sovrac.zig` -> **`GOLDEN-1572`** (Sovra Native Compiler v1.0)\n- `ops/runtime/invalid_test.sovra` -> Hard Compiler Type Error Demonstration\n- `ops/runtime/valid_test.sovra` -> Certified Machine Code Generation Demonstration\n","Description":"Create learning proposal for user review as required by /learn workflow.","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"/Volumes/Untitled/SSOT_Agentic_Brain_v1.1.0_ENGINEERING_RELEASE/docs/plans/learning_proposal.md","toolAction":"Creating learning proposal document","toolSummary":"Write docs/plans/learning_proposal.md"}}]}
